# Version Fingerprinting

## Purpose
Defines version fingerprinting patterns to ensure Cursor and debugging systems can detect when code has been updated and isn't using cached versions.

## Scope
This rule covers fingerprint generation, cache detection, debugging integration, and automation for version tracking.

## Version Fingerprinting Requirements

### Core Principle
**Every script MUST include a unique fingerprint that changes with each version to detect cache issues and ensure console logs match the actual running code.**

### When to Update Fingerprint
```lua
-- ✅ REQUIRED - Update fingerprint for ANY change:
-- - Version increments
-- - Code modifications
-- - Configuration changes
-- - Bug fixes
-- - New features
-- - Performance improvements
-- - Documentation updates
```

## Fingerprint Implementation Patterns

### Basic Fingerprint Pattern
```lua
--[=====[
[[SND Metadata]]
author: 'Your Name'
version: 1.0.0
description: Brief description of what the macro does
plugin_dependencies:
- PluginName1
configs:
  SettingName:
    default: "defaultValue"
    description: What this setting does
[[End Metadata]]
--]=====]

-- Version Fingerprint: v1.0.0-20240115-143022-abc123
-- Generated: 2024-01-15 14:30:22
-- Hash: abc123def456789

-- Version History
-- v1.0.0 - Initial version

-- Your Lua code here
```

### Fingerprint Components
```lua
-- Version Fingerprint Format: v{VERSION}-{DATE}-{TIME}-{HASH}
-- Example: v1.0.1-20240115-143022-abc123

-- Components:
-- v{VERSION}     - Semantic version (1.0.1)
-- {DATE}         - YYYYMMDD format (20240115)
-- {TIME}         - HHMMSS format (143022)
-- {HASH}         - Short hash of code changes (abc123)
```

## Fingerprint Generation Methods

### Method 1: Timestamp-Based Fingerprint
```lua
-- Simple timestamp-based fingerprint
local function GenerateFingerprint(version)
    local timestamp = os.date("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S")
    return "v" .. version .. "-" .. timestamp
end

-- Usage in script
local VERSION_FINGERPRINT = GenerateFingerprint("1.0.1")
-- Result: v1.0.1-20240115-143022
```

### Method 2: Hash-Based Fingerprint
```lua
-- Content hash-based fingerprint
local function GenerateContentHash(content)
    -- Simple hash function (you can use more sophisticated hashing)
    local hash = 0
    for i = 1, #content do
        hash = hash + string.byte(content, i) * i
    end
    return string.format("%06x", hash % 0xFFFFFF)
end

local function GenerateFingerprint(version, content)
    local timestamp = os.date("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S")
    local hash = GenerateContentHash(content)
    return "v" .. version .. "-" .. timestamp .. "-" .. hash
end

-- Usage
local VERSION_FINGERPRINT = GenerateFingerprint("1.0.1", "your code content")
-- Result: v1.0.1-20240115-143022-abc123
```

### Method 3: Automated Fingerprint
```lua
-- Automated fingerprint generation
local function AutoGenerateFingerprint()
    local version = Config.Get("Version") or "1.0.0"
    local timestamp = os.date("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S")
    local random = math.random(100000, 999999)
    return "v" .. version .. "-" .. timestamp .. "-" .. random
end

-- Usage
local VERSION_FINGERPRINT = AutoGenerateFingerprint()
```

## Fingerprint Integration Patterns

### Console Logging with Fingerprint
```lua
-- Always include fingerprint in console logs
local function LogWithFingerprint(message)
    local fingerprint = VERSION_FINGERPRINT or "unknown"
    yield("/echo [" .. fingerprint .. "] " .. message)
end

-- Usage
LogWithFingerprint("Script started")
LogWithFingerprint("Processing items...")
LogWithFingerprint("Script completed")
```

### Debug Information with Fingerprint
```lua
-- Include fingerprint in debug information
local function LogDebugInfo()
    local fingerprint = VERSION_FINGERPRINT or "unknown"
    local version = Config.Get("Version") or "unknown"
    
    yield("/echo [DEBUG] Version: " .. version)
    yield("/echo [DEBUG] Fingerprint: " .. fingerprint)
    yield("/echo [DEBUG] Timestamp: " .. os.date("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"))
    yield("/echo [DEBUG] Player: " .. (Player.Name or "Unknown"))
end
```

### Cache Detection
```lua
-- Check if code is cached by comparing fingerprints
local function CheckCacheStatus()
    local currentFingerprint = VERSION_FINGERPRINT
    local lastKnownFingerprint = Config.Get("LastKnownFingerprint")
    
    if lastKnownFingerprint and lastKnownFingerprint ~= currentFingerprint then
        yield("/echo [CACHE] Code updated! New fingerprint: " .. currentFingerprint)
        yield("/echo [CACHE] Previous fingerprint: " .. lastKnownFingerprint)
        -- Update stored fingerprint
        Config.Set("LastKnownFingerprint", currentFingerprint)
    elseif not lastKnownFingerprint then
        yield("/echo [CACHE] First run with fingerprint: " .. currentFingerprint)
        Config.Set("LastKnownFingerprint", currentFingerprint)
    else
        yield("/echo [CACHE] Using cached version: " .. currentFingerprint)
    end
end
```

## Automated Fingerprint Management

### Cursor Integration
```lua
-- When Cursor detects code changes, automatically:
-- 1. Generate new fingerprint
-- 2. Update fingerprint in script
-- 3. Update version if needed
-- 4. Log fingerprint change

-- Example automation trigger:
-- File saved → Generate fingerprint → Update script → Log change
```

### Version Synchronization
```lua
-- Ensure fingerprint matches version
local function SyncFingerprintWithVersion()
    local version = Config.Get("Version") or "1.0.0"
    local currentFingerprint = VERSION_FINGERPRINT
    
    -- Check if fingerprint version matches script version
    local fingerprintVersion = string.match(currentFingerprint, "v([^-]+)")
    if fingerprintVersion ~= version then
        yield("/echo [SYNC] Version mismatch detected!")
        yield("/echo [SYNC] Script version: " .. version)
        yield("/echo [SYNC] Fingerprint version: " .. fingerprintVersion)
        -- Regenerate fingerprint with correct version
        VERSION_FINGERPRINT = GenerateFingerprint(version)
    end
end
```

## Fingerprint Validation

### Pre-Execution Validation
```lua
-- Validate fingerprint before script execution
local function ValidateFingerprint()
    if not VERSION_FINGERPRINT then
        yield("/echo [ERROR] No version fingerprint found!")
        yield("/echo [ERROR] Script may be using cached version")
        return false
    end
    
    -- Check fingerprint format
    if not string.match(VERSION_FINGERPRINT, "^v%d+%.%d+%.%d+%-%d+%-%d+%-%w+$") then
        yield("/echo [ERROR] Invalid fingerprint format: " .. VERSION_FINGERPRINT)
        return false
    end
    
    yield("/echo [VALID] Fingerprint validated: " .. VERSION_FINGERPRINT)
    return true
end
```

### Runtime Fingerprint Checking
```lua
-- Check fingerprint during script execution
local function CheckRuntimeFingerprint()
    local expectedFingerprint = VERSION_FINGERPRINT
    local actualFingerprint = Config.Get("RuntimeFingerprint")
    
    if actualFingerprint and actualFingerprint ~= expectedFingerprint then
        yield("/echo [WARNING] Runtime fingerprint mismatch!")
        yield("/echo [WARNING] Expected: " .. expectedFingerprint)
        yield("/echo [WARNING] Actual: " .. actualFingerprint)
        yield("/echo [WARNING] Code may be cached or modified")
    end
end
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Always Include Fingerprint
```lua
-- ✅ GOOD - Always include fingerprint
local VERSION_FINGERPRINT = "v1.0.1-20240115-143022-abc123"

-- ❌ BAD - No fingerprint
-- Script without fingerprint
```

### 2. Update Fingerprint with Changes
```lua
-- ✅ GOOD - Update fingerprint when making changes
-- Version Fingerprint: v1.0.1-20240115-143022-abc123
-- Make code change
-- Version Fingerprint: v1.0.2-20240115-143045-def456

-- ❌ BAD - Same fingerprint after changes
-- Version Fingerprint: v1.0.1-20240115-143022-abc123
-- Make code change
-- Version Fingerprint: v1.0.1-20240115-143022-abc123 (unchanged)
```

### 3. Use Fingerprint in Logs
```lua
-- ✅ GOOD - Include fingerprint in logs
yield("/echo [v1.0.1-20240115-143022-abc123] Script started")

-- ❌ BAD - No fingerprint in logs
yield("/echo Script started")
```

### 4. Validate Fingerprints
```lua
-- ✅ GOOD - Validate fingerprint format
if string.match(VERSION_FINGERPRINT, "^v%d+%.%d+%.%d+%-%d+%-%d+%-%w+$") then
    -- Valid fingerprint
end

-- ❌ BAD - No validation
-- Assume fingerprint is always valid
```

## Error Prevention

### Common Fingerprint Mistakes
```lua
-- ❌ AVOID - Forgetting to update fingerprint
-- Making code changes without updating fingerprint

-- ❌ AVOID - Invalid fingerprint format
-- VERSION_FINGERPRINT = "invalid-format"

-- ❌ AVOID - Same fingerprint for different versions
-- v1.0.1 and v1.0.2 using same fingerprint

-- ❌ AVOID - Missing fingerprint validation
-- Not checking if fingerprint exists or is valid
```

### Fingerprint Validation Rules
```lua
-- Automated checks should verify:
-- 1. Fingerprint is present in script
-- 2. Fingerprint format is valid
-- 3. Fingerprint version matches script version
-- 4. Fingerprint is updated when code changes
-- 5. Fingerprint is included in console logs
```

